<COMMENT>
And here is a slight generalisation of this definition.

<DEFN name="Noncentral $\chi^2$-distribution">If <M>U_1,...,U_k</M>  are independent
 <M>N(\mu_i,1),</M>  then the distribution of <M>\sum_{i=1}^k
 U_i^2</M>  is called <TERM>noncentral chi-square</TERM>  with <M>k</M>  <TERM>degrees of
 freedom</TERM>  and <TERM>noncentrality</TERM>  <M>\sum_{i=1}^k \mu_i^2.</M>. This distribution is
sometimes  denoted by <M>\k k(*(\sum_i \mu_i^2)*)</M>.</DEFN>
</COMMENT>
-------EOD-------
</COMMENT>
